  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1046 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nDespite another chilly morning on Tuesday, warming temperatures are \nlikely through this week as upper ridging and southerly flow becomes \nre-established over the region. This will also tend to create breezy \nafternoon winds, especially Tuesday and Wednesday. A progressive \nupper level wave will pass through the central and northern plains \non Wednesday. In response, a few light showers cannot be ruled out \nWednesday night into Thursday across eastern Oklahoma, but otherwise \nthe forecast remains dry for much of this week. High temperatures \nwill continue to warm and, by Friday, most locations may exceed 70 \ndegrees.\n\nAttention then turns to a stronger system projected to impact the\nregion next weekend. Latest trends suggest the upper system might\ntrack further north, though the vast majority of guidance still \nbrings the associated cold front through the CWA. There is plenty\nof time for things to change, but the overall theme of increasing\nrain chances and potential for colder temperatures going into \nnext week remains.",
